etail":"總負債資產比率 = 16.8%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 3.83"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":131.23,"default_fair_val":131.23,"premium_pct":-24.2,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":8.9,"pe_forward":7.8,"pb_trailing":2.6,"pb_forward":2.3,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":3.8,"fcf_to_ev":8.82,"fcf_to_mcap":6.64,"liab_to_assets":16.8,"cash_to_assets":53.4,"current_ratio":3.83,"roe":28.8,"roa":24,"moat":{"ticker":"ZM","period":"2027Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Zoom 在視訊通訊領域建立了強大的品牌認知度，其名稱幾乎成為該類別的代名詞。這種品牌力量使其在定價上具有一定的彈性，能夠收取高於競爭對手的價格，尤其是在企業級市場。然而，視訊通訊領域的競爭激烈，新進入者和現有科技巨頭的產品不斷湧現，這限制了其絕對的定價權。其品牌壁壘相對堅固，但並非無懈可擊。","comment_en":"Zoom has established strong brand recognition in video communications, with its name becoming almost synonymous with the category. This brand equity allows for some pricing flexibility, enabling it to charge a premium, particularly in the enterprise segment. However, the competitive landscape is intense, with new entrants and established tech giants constantly innovating, which caps its absolute pricing power. The brand moat is relatively solid but not impregnable."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Zoom 的核心技術主要基於軟體和演算法，雖然擁有相關專利，但這類技術的專利壁壘相對較弱且容易被規避或模仿。視訊通訊領域的監管風險較低，但專利保護並非其主要的競爭優勢。與製藥或特定硬體製造商相比，其專利壁壘的持久性和強度明顯不足。","comment_en":"Zoom's core technology relies on software and algorithms. While it holds patents, the patent moat in this area is relatively weak and susceptible to circumvention or imitation. Regulatory risks are low in video communications, but patent protection is not its primary competitive advantage. Compared to industries like pharmaceuticals or specific hardware manufacturing, the durability and strength of its patent moat are significantly less pronounced."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"對於企業用戶而言，將 Zoom 整合到現有的工作流程和 IT 基礎設施中需要時間和資源，這構成了一定的轉換成本。員工習慣了 Zoom 的介面和功能，重新培訓和適應新平台也會帶來不便。然而，由於市場上存在許多功能相似且易於部署的替代方案，這些轉換成本並不足以形成極高的壁壘，用戶仍有較大的選擇空間。","comment_en":"For enterprise users, integrating Zoom into existing workflows and IT infrastructure involves time and resources, creating moderate switching costs. Employee familiarity with Zoom's interface and features means retraining and adapting to a new platform can be inconvenient. However, the availability of numerous similar and easily deployable alternatives limits these costs from becoming prohibitively high, leaving users with considerable choice."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Zoom 展現了顯著的網絡效應。當越來越多的聯繫人、客戶和合作夥伴使用 Zoom 時，其對現有用戶的價值就越大，因為他們可以更方便地與更多人進行聯繫。這種效應在企業協作和遠程教育等領域尤為明顯，形成了一個正向循環，增加了用戶黏性並吸引新用戶加入。","comment_en":"Zoom exhibits notable network effects. As more contacts, clients, and partners use Zoom, its value increases for existing users due to the ease of connecting with a larger network. This is particularly evident in enterprise collaboration and remote education, creating a virtuous cycle that enhances user stickiness and attracts new users."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Zoom 作為領先的視訊通訊平台，透過其龐大的用戶基礎和營運規模，在基礎設施和技術研發上實現了一定的成本優勢。大規模部署使其能夠更有效地分攤固定成本。然而，雲端基礎設施的邊際成本相對較低，且競爭對手也能透過規模經濟降低成本，因此 Zoom 的成本優勢並非壓倒性的，但仍是其競爭力的重要組成部分。","comment_en":"As a leading video communication platform, Zoom leverages its vast user base and operational scale to achieve some cost advantages in infrastructure and R&D. Large-scale deployment allows for more efficient fixed cost absorption. However, the marginal cost of cloud infrastructure is relatively low, and competitors can also achieve economies of scale. Thus, Zoom's cost advantage is not overwhelming but remains a significant component of its competitiveness."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Zoom 的業務本質上是全球性的軟體服務，不依賴於特定的地理位置或獨特的實體資產。其競爭優勢來自於技術、品牌和網絡效應，而非地理位置的稀缺性。因此，在這一維度上，Zoom 並不具備顯著的護城河。","comment_en":"Zoom's business is inherently a global software service, not reliant on specific geographic locations or unique physical assets. Its competitive advantages stem from technology, brand, and network effects, rather than geographical scarcity. Consequently, Zoom possesses no significant moat in this dimension."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Zoom 在提供穩定、高品質的視訊會議服務方面展現了卓越的營運效率。其平台能夠支持大規模並發連接，並保持低延遲和高可靠性，這對於用戶體驗至關重要。疫情期間的快速擴張證明了其營運韌性和擴展能力。這種高效的營運能力是其核心競爭力之一，尤其是在保證服務質量方面。","comment_en":"Zoom demonstrates exceptional operational efficiency in delivering stable, high-quality video conferencing. Its platform supports massive concurrent connections with low latency and high reliability, crucial for user experience. The rapid scaling during the pandemic highlighted its operational resilience and capacity. This efficiency is a core competitive strength, especially in ensuring service quality."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Zoom 擁有健康的現金流和充裕的現金儲備，並相對謹慎地管理其債務。公司在研發投入、市場拓展和潛在的戰略收購之間進行了較為明智的資本配置。其較高的 ROE 和 ROA 反映了有效的資本運用。儘管尚未進行大規模的戰略性併購，但其財務狀況為未來的戰略選擇提供了堅實基礎。","comment_en":"Zoom possesses strong cash flow and ample cash reserves, managing its debt relatively conservatively. The company has allocated capital prudently between R&D investment, market expansion, and potential strategic acquisitions. Its high ROE and ROA indicate effective capital utilization. While no large-scale strategic M&A has occurred, its financial health provides a solid foundation for future strategic options."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Zoom 的客戶留存率相對較高，這得益於其強大的品牌、用戶習慣以及網絡效應。一旦企業將 Zoom 整合到日常運營中，並且員工習慣了其易用性，轉換到其他平台的意願就會降低。持續的產品創新和對客戶反饋的響應也進一步鞏固了客戶關係，使其能夠在競爭激烈的市場中保持穩定的客戶基礎。","comment_en":"Zoom enjoys relatively high customer retention, driven by its strong brand, user habits, and network effects. Once enterprises integrate Zoom into daily operations and employees become accustomed to its ease of use, the willingness to switch to other platforms diminishes. Continuous product innovation and responsiveness to customer feedback further solidify customer relationships, enabling a stable customer base in a competitive market."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Zoom 的核心業務在後疫情時代面臨挑戰，遠程辦公模式的常態化程度不如預期，導致其增長放緩。雖然視訊通訊作為一種工具具有持久性，但 Zoom 作為單一平台的持久性面臨來自微軟 Teams、Google Meet 等整合性平台的激烈競爭。其技術和商業模式的可持續性有待觀察，尤其是在面對不斷變化的市場需求和技術發展時。","comment_en":"Zoom's core business faces post-pandemic challenges as the normalization of remote work proves less pervasive than initially expected, leading to slower growth. While video communication as a tool is durable, Zoom's durability as a standalone platform is challenged by integrated offerings from Microsoft Teams, Google Meet, and others. The sustainability of its technology and business model remains to be seen, especially against evolving market demands and technological advancements."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Zoom 在視訊通訊領域建立了強大的品牌聲譽和顯著的網絡效應，使其在 M4 和 M1 的評分較高。其營運效率（M7）和客戶留存率（M9）也表現出色，顯示了其作為協作工具的價值。然而，其護城河並非無懈可擊，專利壁壘（M2）薄弱，且面臨來自大型科技公司整合平台的激烈競爭，這影響了其定價權（M1）和業務的持久性（M10）。總體而言，Zoom 擁有一個相對堅固但非永久性的『收費橋』式護城河，其價值在於連接的便利性和用戶習慣，但易受技術變革和平台整合的挑戰。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Zoom possesses a strong brand reputation and significant network effects in video communications, reflected in its high scores for M4 and M1. Its operational efficiency (M7) and customer retention (M9) are also notable, highlighting its value as a collaboration tool. However, its moat is not impregnable. Weak patent barriers (M2) and intense competition from integrated platforms by tech giants challenge its pricing power (M1) and business durability (M10). Overall, Zoom has a relatively solid, but not perpetual, 'toll bridge' style moat, deriving value from connection convenience and user habits, yet susceptible to technological shifts and platform integration.","evidenceHash":"782d3f9b9bc8d55f50a49d8ca85f65e02f9726b415414bda78ac887237f67c20","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":8,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-01-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:40:26.418Z","evidenceHash":"54cff5f2ea3d5cb3fe195540f6988fb53eb10144e536ecc028dbbdcfb8ca15d4"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-01-31","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:40:26.418Z","evidenceHash":"54cff5f2ea3d5cb3fe195540f6988fb53eb10144e536ecc028dbbdcfb8ca15d4"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/ZM.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/ZM.png","website":"https://www.zoom.com","ceo":"Eric S. Yuan","full_time_employees":"7438","description":"Zoom Communications, Inc. provides a robust platform for enhancing communication and fostering collaboration. The company's global reach is organized into three primary operational regions: the Americas, the Asia Pacific, and Europe, the Middle East, and Africa (EMEA). Eric S. Yuan founded the enterprise in 2011, and its corporate headquarters are situated in San Jose, California.","description_en":"Zoom Communications, Inc. provides a robust platform for enhancing communication and fostering collaboration. The company's global reach is organized into three primary operational regions: the Americas, the Asia Pacific, and Europe, the Middle East, and Africa (EMEA). Eric S. Yuan founded the enterprise in 2011, and its corporate headquarters are situated in San Jose, California.","description_zh":"**Zoom Communications, Inc. (ZM) 業務營運概述**\n\nZoom Communications, Inc. (ZM) 是一家領先的通訊協作平台供應商，致力於提供強健的解決方案，以增強全球企業的溝通與協作能力。公司營運遍及全球，主要劃分為三大區域：美洲、亞太地區，以及歐洲、中東與非洲 (EMEA)。\n\n其核心產品為基於雲端的視訊會議及通訊平台，提供高品質的視訊、音訊會議、線上研討會、聊天、電話服務及協作工具。Zoom 的關鍵技術在於其穩定可靠的網路傳輸技術，即使在頻寬受限的環境下，也能提供流暢的視訊體驗。\n\n營運模式上，Zoom 主要採取軟體即服務 (SaaS) 的訂閱制收費模式，向個人用戶、小型企業、中大型企業及教育機構提供不同層級的付費方案。此外，公司亦透過 API 整合，與眾多第三方應用程式建立生態系，擴展其服務範疇與客戶黏著度。Zoom 創立於 2011 年，總部位於美國加州聖荷西。","address":"55 Almaden Boulevard","city":"San Jose","state":"CA","zip":"95113","country":"US","phone":"888 799 9666","full_address":"55 Almaden Boulevard, San Jose, CA 95113, US","range_52w":"70.7-114.74","year_high":114.74,"year_low":70.7,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":70.7,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"McGarry Kimberly J","title":"officer: Chief Accounting Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":3121,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"McGarry Kimberly J","title":"officer: Chief Accounting Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":3121,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"McGarry Kimberly J","title":"officer: Chief Accounting Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":1383,"price":94.67,"total_val":0.13},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"McGarry Kimberly J","title":"officer: Chief Accounting Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":8692,"price":97.56,"total_val":0.85},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"Chang Michelle","title":"officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":22218,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"Chang Michelle","title":"officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":22218,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"Chang Michelle","title":"officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":8743,"price":94.67,"total_val":0.83},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"Chang Michelle","title":"officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":2742,"price":98.67,"total_val":0.27},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"Chang Michelle","title":"officer: Chief Financial Offi